{"Title":"Proposal for a legislative amendment to the Constitution relative to changing the mandatory age of retirement for judges","BillNumber":"H36","DocketNumber":"HD3206","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T10:53:25.23"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T10:53:25.23"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H36/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Proposal for Constitutional Amendment","Pinslip":"By Representative McMurtry of Dedham, a petition (accompanied by proposal for constitutional amendment, House, No. 36) of Paul McMurtry for a legislative amendment to the Constitution relative to changing the mandatory age of retirement for judges.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tArticle I of Chapter III of Part the Second of the Constitution of the Commonwealth is hereby amended by striking out the word “seventy” and inserting in place thereof the following figure:- 75.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Adverse","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}